<title>NETHERLANDS: IHC CALAND REITERATES 1997 FORECAST.</title>
<headline>IHC CALAND REITERATES 1997 FORECAST.</headline>
<dateline>SCHIEDAM, Netherlands 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipbuilding and engineering group IHC Caland NV on Monday repeated its forecast of an 18 percent increase in full-year 1997 net profit.</p>
<p>&quot;Based on the current order portfolio and viable projects in the promising markets in which the group operates, management expects 1997 group net profit will rise by about 18 percent to some 110 million guilders,&quot; IHC Caland said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company said in January it expected the 1997 net profit to rise by 18 percent to about 110 million guilders and earnings per share to grow by about 12 percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
